" (https://www.dps.texas.gov/internetforms/Forms/DL-60.pdf)\nciteturn25view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 2; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.dps.texas.gov/internetforms/Forms/DL-60.pdf\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 172\nL0@P0: www.dps.texas.gov/DriverLicense\nL1@P0: Safety Tips\nL2@P0: Please follow these general safety tips when\nL3@P0: operating a vehicle:\nL4@P0:  Always drive defensively. Try to anticipate errors\nL5@P0: another driver might make.\nL6@P0:  Be aware of your surroundings. Check your\nL7@P0: mirrors, look both ways at intersections, and look\nL8@P0: over the proper shoulder before making a lane\nL9@P0: change or merging with traffic.\nL10@P0:  Steer smoothly and avoid sudden turns.\nL11@P0:  Accelerate and stop smoothly. Slow down or\nL12@P0: speed up gradually to avoid sudden jerks.\nL13@P0:  Be aware of where you have to stop when\nL14@P0: approaching an intersection. If your view is\nL15@P0: blocked, stop, then move forward carefully. Look\nL16@P0: both ways before continuing into the intersection.\nL17@P0: Do not roll through stop signs or red lights.\nL18@P0:  Always obey posted speed limits. When poor\nL19@P0: weather, road, or traffic conditions are present,\nL20@P0: reduce speed accordingly.\nL21@P0:  Use the two-second rule to ensure you are\nL22@P0: following at a safe distance. Increase the\nL23@P0: following distance for poor weather, road, or\nL24@P0: traffic conditions.\nL25@P0:  Know what all traffic signs and signals mean and\nL26@P0: obey them at all times.\nL27@P0:  Use the correct lane. If you are in the improper\nL28@P0: lane, signal and turn into the proper lane.\nL29@P0:  Put your signal on 100 feet before turning or\nL30@P0: changing lanes.\nL31@P0: Driver Safety Checklist\nL32@P0: Before Starting the Vehicle\nL33@P0:  Adjust the mirrors and your seat\nL34@P0:  Fasten your seat belt\nL35@P0:  Know where the vehicle controls are located\nL36@P0:  and how to use them (headlights,\nL37@P0:  windshield wipers, turn signals, etc.)\nL38@P0: During the Drive Test\nL39@P0:  Use the turn signals when appropriate\nL40@P0:  Look in the mirrors regularly and over your\nL41@P0:  shoulder when necessary\nL42@P0:  Keep both hands on the steering wheel\nL43@P0:  unless you are backing up\nL44@P0: Stopping\nL45@P0:  Check traffic\nL46@P0:  Stop completely behind crosswalk or limit\nL47@P0:  line\nL48@P0:  Stop smoothly without the vehicle “jerking”\nL49@P0: Turning or Changing Lanes\nL50@P0:  Signal 100 feet before starting maneuver\nL51@P0:  Adjust speed for safety\nL52@P0:  Check mirrors\nL53@P0:  Look over your shoulder for the blind spot\nL54@P0:  Begin and end maneuver in correct lane\nL55@P0:  Yield or accept right-of-way as appropriate\nL56@P0: Always\nL57@P0:  Check mirrors at regular intervals\nL58@P0:  Look both ways at all intersections\nL59@P0:  Look for and obey all traffic lights and signs\nL60@P0:  See and react appropriately to hazards\nL61@P0:  Follow at a safe distance (adjust for\nL62@P0: weather)\nL63@P0: To empower the citizens of our state with trusted\nL64@P0: credentials that enable security, mobility and opportunity.\nL65@P0: DRIVER LICENSE DIVISION\nL66@P0: Driver License (DL)\nL67@P0: How to Prepare\nL68@P0: for a Drive Test\nL69@P0: DL-60 rev. 03-2026\nL70@P0: Help keep Texans safe.\nL71@P0-1: Be a responsible driver. Who Must Take the Drive Test?\nL72@P1: You are required to take a drive test if any of the\nL73@P1: following conditions apply:\nL74@P1:  You have never been licensed in any U.S. state\nL75@P1: or territory.\nL76@P1:  You are licensed in another state, but your\nL77@P1: license has been expired over two years.\nL78@P1:  You are licensed in Texas, but your license has\nL79@P1: been expired over two years.\nL80@P1:  You have a medical condition that may affect\nL81@P1: your ability to safely operate a vehicle.\nL82@P1:  You currently have specific restrictions on your\nL83@P1: Texas driver license which require a driving test\nL84@P1: to be removed.\nL85@P1:  You were ordered by a court to comply with a\nL86@P1: driving test.\nL87@P1: A drive test is not required for renewals or for anyone\nL88@P1: over age 18 surrendering a valid driver license or\nL89@P1: license not expired over two years from another\nL90@P1: state; however, DPS may require a drive test at any\nL91@P1: time. Anyone under age 18 must take a driving test.\nL92@P1: Preparing for the Drive Test\nL93@P1: To prepare for the drive test, review the Texas Driver\nL94@P1: Handbook. This free handbook is available online at\nL95@P1: https://www.dps.texas.gov/internetforms/\nL96@P1: getForm.ashx?id=DL-7.pdf\nL97@P1: Practice all of the maneuvers listed in the “Driver\nL98@P1: Safety Checklist” section before scheduling your test.\nL99@P1: While practicing, ask the person with you to give you\nL100@P1: instructions and point out any mistakes.\nL101@P1: Scheduling a Drive Test\nL102@P1: All Driver License offices now offer the\nL103@P1: option of scheduling your drive test online.\nL104@P1: To schedule a drive test, visit\nL105@P1: https://public.txdpsscheduler.com\nL106@P1: Vehicle Inspection\nL107@P1: Before you begin the drive test, the vehicle you bring\nL108@P1: must pass an inspection to ensure it is safe and can\nL109@P1: be legally operated on public roadways.\nL110@P1: The License and Permit Specialist will check for:\nL111@P1: \nL112@P1:  Two license plates with the exception of single\nL113@P1: out-of-state or temporary plates; no auto\nL114@P1: dealership plates\nL115@P1: (permanently affixed to the front and back of the\nL116@P1: vehicle)\nL117@P1:  Operational speedometer\nL118@P1:  A properly functioning horn\nL119@P1:  Turn signals on the front and back of the vehicle\nL120@P1:  Unexpired vehicle registration and inspection\nL121@P1:  Unexpired insurance\nL122@P1: (applicant cannot be listed as “excluded driver”)\nL123@P1:  At least one rearview mirror inside or outside of\nL124@P1: the vehicle\nL125@P1:  Driver and front passenger door must open\nL126@P1: normally\nL127@P1:  Functioning seatbelts\nL128@P1:  Brake lights\nL129@P1:  Windshield wipers, headlights, and taillights,\nL130@P1: depending on weather conditions and time of day\nL131@P1:  Any restrictions on the driver license\nL132@P1: Before the Drive Test\nL133@P1: You must present one valid form of identification to\nL134@P1: the License and Permit Specialist before the drive\nL135@P1: test.\nL136@P1: Try to ask all questions before your drive test begins.\nL137@P1: Once the test starts, the License and\nL138@P1: Permit Specialist is not permitted\nL139@P1: to engage in general conversation.\nL140@P1: During the Drive Test\nL141@P1: No pets or unauthorized passengers are allowed in\nL142@P1: the vehicle during the test.\nL143@P1: The test takes about 20 minutes. The goals of the\nL144@P1: drive test are to determine your ability to safely\nL145@P1: operate a vehicle and obey traffic laws.\nL146@P1: You will be graded on your ability to demonstrate the\nL147@P1: following maneuvers:\nL148@P1:  Backing in a straight line\nL149@P1:  Parallel parking\nL150@P1:  Approaching intersections\nL151@P1:  Turning\nL152@P1:  Stopping in regular traffic conditions\nL153@P1:  Controlling the vehicle\nL154@P1:  Observing traffic\nL155@P1:  Maintaining vehicle position (turning, stopping,\nL156@P1: etc.)\nL157@P1:  Using signals\nL158@P1: If at any time a dangerous or illegal maneuver is\nL159@P1: performed, the drive test will be immediately stopped\nL160@P1: and will result in an automatic failure.\nL161@P1: After the Drive Test\nL162@P1: After you complete the drive test, you will be\nL163@P1: informed if you passed or failed. You will also receive\nL164@P1: detailed feedback on the areas where you did well\nL165@P1: and the areas where you need to improve.\nL166@P1: If you do not pass the drive test, your application will\nL167@P1: be held in the driver license office for 90 days. After\nL168@P1: 90 days ─ or three failed tests ─ a new application and\nL169@P1: fee must be submitted.\nL170@P1: Becoming a safe driver\nL171@P1: is an ongoing process.\n"
